spec: S06-13

`profile add | remove` on config.toml (a group of its own: it adds profiles while it runs and
removes them again). There is no default profile: a call without -p is exit 3, naming the
profiles. Tokens are never printed. Merged stdout+stderr.

```console
$ annotary -p rowan profile add tmp --server http://127.0.0.1:1 --token ant_notreal
profile "tmp" saved → [..]/config.toml

$ annotary -p rowan profile add tmp --server http://127.0.0.1:1
? 5
error: profile 'tmp' already exists in [..]/config.toml — `annotary profile remove NAME` first, or `annotary login -p NAME` to replace its token

$ annotary -p rowan profile add tmp2 --vault notes
profile "tmp2" has no token yet — `annotary login -p tmp2` fills it
profile "tmp2" saved → [..]/config.toml

$ annotary -p rowan profile add tmp3 --server ftp://nope
? 1
error: --server "ftp://nope" must be an http(s) URL

$ annotary member list
? 3
error: no credential — say who you are: pass -p NAME (`annotary profile list` shows whose each one is), or set ANNOTARY_TOKEN
profiles in ~/.annotary/config.toml: agent, down, limited, pw, rowan, tmp, tmp2

$ annotary -p rowan profile remove tmp
profile "tmp" removed → [..]/config.toml

$ annotary -p rowan profile remove tmp2 --json
{"name":"tmp2","server":"http://127.0.0.1:7377","vault":"notes"}

$ annotary -p rowan profile remove tmp
? 2
error: profile 'tmp' not found in ~/.annotary/config.toml — profiles: agent, down, limited, pw, rowan

```
